From a8d78db327a4d3119b4c98f7e84f8928e5a4e9e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 01:32:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/9] Tier 1: aggregates returned in the x87's registers (#141)

A struct of a long double comes back in st0 and a _Complex long double
in st0 and st1, each part 16 bytes of the aggregate
(tier1_select_x87_parts). A call stores st0 into the first part and
then st1 into the second (fstp); a function's return loads them the
last first (fld), so that st0 holds the first. A long double argument of
a call with ABI records takes its stack slots as a plain one does.

The two anchors that relied on the refusal move to a naked function,
whose body is assembly that admission leaves to Tier 0: the outcome
test's mixed fixture and the multicore driver test's widen.

test-checker-driver gains the wide values' fixture: long doubles, x87
aggregates, a memory-class result and a variadic definition's va_arg of
long double, beside 128-bit integers within its bodies, crossing to and
from clang -O2's code, every function Tier 1's by both paths, against
clang -O0's build. c-testsuite's subset now compiles 430 of its 430
functions by Tier 1.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TiDLnvjnrjwbym9rZvTaVA
