From 97806049dd8b842471bf7d1d432acdc20647b408 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 09:57:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] Tier 1: one scan for vectors per function (#141)

The vectors' commit scanned each function for vectors three times
(ir_function_has_vectors_path): selection, for its candidates, and the
CFG consumer twice, for its chain check and for its problem's classes
and sizes. On the frozen sqlite3.c, which has none, those scans took
about 1.6M of the 10.3M instructions that commit added to the
--tier1 -c compile (an instruction profile on the 9700X below perf's
throttling rate). Selection's scan now rides the plan
(Tier1SelectPlan.vectors), and the CFG consumer reads it.

